WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.355 --> 00:00:01.540
(bright music)

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:03.870
- [Narrator] What may seem
like a beautiful oasis,

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:07.396
is actually the top of an active volcano.

00:00:07.396 --> 00:00:09.979
(bright music)

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:17.490
Located in Java, Indonesia,
is the Kawah Ijen volcano.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:20.913
At its top sits a crater lake
filled with hydrochloric acid.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:24.910
The water is 90 degrees
Fahrenheit and appears

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:26.100
a blueish green.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.720
No species lives in or around the water,

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.923
as the conditions are too
harsh for nature to survive.

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:36.960
At night a rare phenomenon can be seen.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:40.020
Unlike any other volcano
in the world, Kawah Ijen

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:43.200
emits what appears to
be bright blue flames.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.670
This blue glow is not caused by lava,

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:49.640
but instead from a combustion
of sulfuric gasses.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:52.810
Ones the gasses cool, a
bright yellow sulfur forms,

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:55.320
which is mined and sold.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.750
Miners use steel bars to break
off portions of the sulfur,

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:01.743
and carry up to 200 pounds
back down the volcano.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.490
The emitted gasses are toxic if inhaled,

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:08.713
making this strenuous
work incredibly dangerous.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:11.620
While this unique volcano maybe home

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:13.720
to one of the world's most grueling jobs,

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:16.913
it is also a sight worth seeing.

00:01:16.913 --> 00:01:19.580
(bright music)

